WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.120
The additive calendar model gives each
hour its own effect and adds one shared

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.650
working day adjustment.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.230
Holding the other inputs fixed,

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.050
that day type adjustment is the same at
eight in the morning and two at night.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.770
Our observations suggest those differences
may need distinct hourly shapes.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.520
A new optimizer or another scale cannot
create a product that is absent from the

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.050
model.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.540
We make that relationship explicit in the
representation and compare it under the

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.130
same training least squares solver.

00:00:37.192 --> 00:00:42.242
We retain every original calendar
column and append twenty four products.

00:00:42.952 --> 00:00:46.682
Each multiplies one hour
indicator by the working day flag.

00:00:47.492 --> 00:00:51.842
For the real Monday at eight,
the hour eight product is one,

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:54.102
and the other new products are zero.

00:00:55.092 --> 00:00:57.272
Its declared position
is index fifty three,

00:00:57.272 --> 00:00:59.762
after the original forty five columns.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:04.382
A nonworking hour has zero
in every appended product.

00:01:05.212 --> 00:01:08.282
The original hour indicators
still remain available.

00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:12.202
The feature construction
uses calendar values only;

00:01:12.912 --> 00:01:15.182
observed rental outcomes do not enter it.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.140
The first twenty four
columns are hour indicators.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.610
The last working day flag
is selected as a column,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.200
preserving broadcasting across rows.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.050
Multiplication creates
the twenty four products,

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.800
and column stacking appends
them to the original design.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:38.430
We then fit training only scales and
solve the same unpenalized squared error

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:39.220
objective.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.610
The saved order matters because valid
dimensions alone cannot reveal a misplaced

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:45.640
coefficient.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.840
No weather or demand
history was introduced,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.840
and the split membership and issue
time contract remain the same.

00:01:54.858 --> 00:01:56.328
In raw coordinates,

00:01:56.698 --> 00:02:02.138
the hourly contribution now contains an
hour effect plus an hour specific product

00:02:02.138 --> 00:02:04.648
coefficient when the day flag is one.

00:02:05.018 --> 00:02:09.958
The working day contrast includes the
shared flag coefficient and that hour

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:11.188
specific term.

00:02:11.678 --> 00:02:14.308
It can therefore differ at eight and two.

00:02:14.738 --> 00:02:17.238
This is additional
representational capacity,

00:02:17.238 --> 00:02:20.168
rather than a faster route
through the old family.

00:02:20.878 --> 00:02:23.348
The design still contains
dependent columns,

00:02:23.718 --> 00:02:27.408
so individual coefficients
are not unique causal effects.

00:02:28.098 --> 00:02:31.068
We assess the fitted function
and its later predictions,

00:02:31.418 --> 00:02:34.148
not a story about one isolated weight.

00:02:36.275 --> 00:02:39.602
Training half squared error
falls from about three thousand,

00:02:39.602 --> 00:02:43.545
one hundred and sixty eight to one
thousand, nine hundred and thirty two.

00:02:44.235 --> 00:02:49.172
Raw validation absolute error improves
to about one hundred and eight point six

00:02:49.172 --> 00:02:49.705
nine.

00:02:50.575 --> 00:02:53.805
The nonnegative version reaches
one hundred point five two.

00:02:54.395 --> 00:02:58.225
Because both representations
use stable training solves,

00:02:58.715 --> 00:03:01.425
this supports a concrete
structural comparison.

00:03:02.095 --> 00:03:07.455
Extra flexibility does not guarantee every
validation row improves or that counts

00:03:07.455 --> 00:03:08.785
become nonnegative.

00:03:09.615 --> 00:03:14.275
The complete raw and clipped predictions
remain saved beside the model and its

00:03:14.275 --> 00:03:15.165
feature schema.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.330
At the busy Monday hour,

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.730
the forecast rises from about one hundred
and seventy five to two hundred and sixty,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.570
closer to target four hundred and twenty.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.050
At the quiet target five,
the raw forecast becomes more negative,

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.690
around minus eighty four.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.624
The group baseline still has lower overall
absolute error at ninety one point five

00:03:39.624 --> 00:03:40.110
seven.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.270
The expanded model can represent groups,

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.330
but its extra fitted calendar effects can
generalize less well to the later period.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.190
This observation does not identify
a single cause of the remaining gap.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:58.210
We retain the stronger reference instead
of selecting the newest model by default.

